# Build context hygiene for infra/Dockerfile (context = repo root).
#
# node_modules is the load-bearing entry: without it, `COPY apps/ apps/` lays
# the HOST's (Windows, pnpm-symlinked) tree over the Linux install done in the
# layer above, and the build dies on `Cannot find module .../vite/bin/vite.js`.
# The rest is weight: the rulebook PDFs alone are ~250 MB of context that the
# image neither wants nor is allowed to ship (§14 — books never ship).

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/

# The owner's rulebooks and local models: never in an image (DESIGN §14/§16)
*.pdf
models/

# Runtime state, backups and secrets
data/
**/data/
uploads/
backups/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vendored at install/build time by apps/web/scripts/vendor-pdfjs.mjs
apps/web/public/pdfjs/

# Test and tooling artefacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
*.log

# VCS, editors, CI
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
